# React Router owns every path below /, so each one has to fall through to
# the app shell rather than Netlify's 404.
#
# It matters most for /payment/callback: Paystack returns the customer there
# as a full cross-site navigation, requested cold from the server with no
# router in memory to catch it. A 404 at that moment is indistinguishable,
# from the customer's side, from a payment that took their money and vanished.
#
# This duplicates the rule in netlify.toml on purpose. netlify.toml lives at
# the repo root and is only read on a git-connected build — it is NOT part of
# dist/, so a manual drag-and-drop deploy of the built folder would ship
# without any redirect at all. This file is copied into dist/ by Vite, so the
# rule travels with the build either way.
#
# Netlify gives netlify.toml precedence where the two overlap. They are the
# same rule, so there is nothing to conflict.

/*    /index.html   200
